---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How We Research and Review Saunas | Backyard Sauna Pro"
  description="Our methodology for comparing sauna products, checking claims, disclosing commercial relationships, and keeping buyer guides current."
  canonical="/how-we-review"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Editorial Standards</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-4">How We Research and Review Saunas</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-600">Our job is to help a homeowner make a better decision while making the limits of our evidence visible.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-8 text-stone-700">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Evidence hierarchy</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>Current manufacturer manuals, technical sheets, warranty terms, and safety instructions.</li>
          <li>Retailer specifications and availability, checked against the manufacturer where possible.</li>
          <li>Codes, standards, and qualified professional guidance for installation topics.</li>
          <li>Attributable owner feedback used to identify patterns, not treated as controlled testing.</li>
          <li>Editorial interpretation that connects those facts to a buyer's space, budget, and priorities.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">What "review" means here</h2>
        <p>Unless a page explicitly documents firsthand access and a repeatable method, a review is a desk-researched buyer analysis. We do not claim a product was tested, installed, measured, or personally used without evidence. Manufacturer claims are labeled or attributed rather than repeated as independent findings.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">How we write</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">We write for people making real decisions. Sentences stay direct, related ideas stay close together, and technical detail ends with a clear takeaway.</p>
        <p>Good guidance needs rhythm, too. Some sentences are short. Others carry the nuance a purchase or installation question deserves. We avoid filler, canned transitions, and generic language that sounds polished but says very little.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">How products are compared</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">Criteria vary by buyer problem but commonly include capacity, exterior dimensions, heater type, electrical requirements, indoor or outdoor rating, materials, warranty, shipping, installation complexity, serviceability, retailer support, and total project cost.</p>
        <p>A ranking should explain who a product suits, who should avoid it, important unknowns, and why its criteria matter. Price is described as subject to change.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Commercial relationships</h2>
        <p>We may earn affiliate commissions or accept clearly disclosed paid collaborations. A commercial relationship does not permit fabricated experience, hidden sponsorship, medical claims, or removal of buyer-fit limitations. Material connections are disclosed on the affected page and, where appropriate, next to the recommendation.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Updates and corrections</h2>
        <p>Product data changes. Pages should carry a last-reviewed date when materially checked. Readers and brands can report outdated specifications, links, images, availability, or disclosures through the <a href="/contact/" class="text-amber-700 underline">contact page</a>. Corrections are evaluated against current source material, not accepted automatically.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-5">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Planning and safety boundary</h2>
        <p class="text-sm">Our calculators and planning guides are educational aids, not engineering, electrical, permit, medical, or safety approval. Follow current manufacturer instructions and use qualified local professionals for final decisions.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
